Hi,

Is there an API in StatET that helps to analyse code?

E.g. I will have a R6Class in R file like this:

library(R6)
library(sicrtask)

MyRTask <- R6Class("MyRTask",
  inherit = RTask,
  public = list(
    rtaskinfo <- RTaskInfo$new(atomic = TRUE),
    in1 = NA,
    in2 = NA,
    out1 = NA,
    initialize_ports = function() {
      self$in1 <- InputPort$new(name = "in1", data_type = Int32)
  self$in2 <- InputPort$new(name = "in2", data_type = Int32, asynchronous =
TRUE)
  self$out1 <- OutputPort$new(name = "out1", data_type = Int32)
    },
    initialize = function() {
      self$initialize_ports()
    },
    execute = function(grp) {
 i = self$in1$get_data(Int32)$values[0]
 if( i == 3 ) self$exit_runner()
  },
  ),
  private = list(
  )
)

I would like to extract information like 'inherit', what arguments
RTaskInfo initialization has.
 or all info about InputPort and OutputPort that are in method
initialize_ports.

Thanks,

Marek

